notes: "Here is one change from start to finish, on the 1BNA slide itself. When I reviewed the deck, my feedback was direct: data plots should be drawn with a professional tool, such as a Python package, from the data, not built inside the slide. A chart drawn inside a slide is one of the strongest sources of the AI look; even here, the agent had already had to patch its labels once, because PowerPoint placed them differently. So the request in the Story was: replace the slide chart with a Matplotlib figure drawn from the CSV, and keep the values, the axis range, the citation and the summary table. On the left is the slide before; on the right, after, at the same scale. The table lists what changed: the numbers now live in the data file and a short plotting script in the project, and the figure is regenerated from them, never retouched. The change was proposed as a transaction, previewed and applied through the shared writer, so it can be reviewed on the next slide."
